    "Bare IANA names like `America/New_York` and `Europe/London` ARE NOT in this list and FAIL validation, even though Rufus would happily accept them. Convert IANA -> friendly name before persisting. `UTC` is valid because Rails also exposes it as a friendly name.",
    "Some friendly names alias to the same IANA zone (e.g. `London` and `Edinburgh` both map to `Europe/London`). Either name is valid; pick the one your users recognize.",
    "`UTC` here is the friendly name. Its IANA value is `Etc/UTC`."
